  "body": "## What changed\n\n**Shared pick primitive** - `crates/app/src/pick/circle.rs` (next to the #692 pick graph): `circle_centre(world, &GeoSel)`, `circle_of_edge(graph, edge)`, `circle_of_run(features, run)` return a `Circle { centre, axis, radius, closed }` or a named `CircleRefusal` (`Straight`, `TooShort`, `NotCircular`, `NotAnEdge`, `Gone`). The edge pick resolves to its **run** (one straight stretch or one arc), so an arc of a filleted rim works too. The fit reuses `feature_arc::fit_arc` and its tolerances, and checks every vertex. A non-circular edge is refused, never guessed. The axis sign is canonical, so a hole in a top face reads +Z. The centre is in the active setup's view frame (#326), the frame the WCS is set in.\n\n**Command + MCP** - `SetWcsAtCircleCentre` (`crates/app/src/commands/wcs_circle.rs`) resolves the circle when the command is created and wraps `SetWcsOrigin` at the centre: one undo step, and undo restores the previous origin. The MCP tool `set_wcs_circle_centre { edge: {model, id}, rotation? }` (`crates/app/src/mcp/wcs_circle.rs`) runs the same command and returns the circle's centre, axis and diameter. The camcraft-mcp skill doc lists the tool. No MCP follow-up is needed.\n\n**WCS page** (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page.rs`, split out of the 1894-line `pages.rs`):\n- Three collapsible sections: *Origin and orientation*, *Quarter turns* and *Anchor on*.\n- The six value fields sit in a two-column grid, label and field on one row, with the fields in one column.\n- The quarter turns are two rows of three equal buttons ([X+ Y+ Z+] / [X- Y- Z-]), plus *Level* and *Set Origin* as two equal halves. Every row spans the pane's width.\n- The anchor grid is a 3x3 compass of equal cells (up to 72 x 30), placed exactly and centred.\n- *Anchor on* has a third choice, **Circle centre**. It shows a \"Pick a circular edge\" toggle and then the result, e.g. \"Circle Ø 20.00 mm, centre (0.00, 0.00, 10.00)\", or \"Not anchored: <reason>\". While the toggle is armed, a viewport click takes feature edges only, one run per click, and hover highlights what a click would take. A landed pick disarms the toggle. Choosing Circle centre disarms the box markers, and the other way round.\n- The Bottom/Middle/Top radios are now a plain \"Z level\" row. Beside the 120 px label column they widened the section past a narrow pane.\n\n**Plumbing** - `CommandKind::SetWcsCircle`, and a new `state_wcs.rs` that also takes over the existing `SetWcs` arm (`state.rs` shrinks). The viewport routes clicks through `wcs_pick.rs` (anchor markers + circle pick), which shortens `interact.rs`. `feature_click::ask` returns the circle ask while armed.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `crates/app/tests/circle_centre.rs` (new, 5 tests) uses a plate with a drilled 8 mm hole (32 chords), off-centre at (5, -3):\n  - `a_drilled_hole_rim_gives_its_true_centre_axis_and_radius`: centre within 1e-6, Ø 8, axis +Z, through a real ray pick, and again with the part moved.\n  - `a_straight_edge_is_refused_by_name`.\n  - `an_elliptical_rim_and_a_face_are_refused_never_guessed`: ellipse gives `NotCircular`, face gives `NotAnEdge`, stale id gives `Gone`.\n  - `the_anchor_command_places_the_origin_and_undo_restores_the_previous_one`: undo, redo, and a refusal never builds a command.\n  - `mcp_set_wcs_circle_centre_anchors_on_a_rim_and_refuses_a_straight_edge`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_page_tests.rs` (structural, no pixels):\n  - `the_page_has_three_sections_and_one_row_fields_in_one_column`\n  - `quarter_turns_are_equal_buttons_filling_the_pane`\n  - `the_anchor_points_are_a_centred_compass_of_equal_cells`\n  - It also holds the three `turn_wcs` tests, moved verbatim from `pages.rs`. The test count is unchanged.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/wcs_circle_tests.rs`:\n  - `a_rim_click_anchors_the_origin_on_its_centre_and_undo_restores_it`: combo, then the pick button, then a viewport click on a boss rim, then G54 at the centre. The page states the circle, and Undo restores (1, 2, 3).\n  - `a_face_is_refused_by_name_and_lands_nothing`\n- Gate (macOS, worktree target):\n  - Ran green: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `camcraft-app --lib`, the full `camcraft-ui` lib and integration suites (459 lib tests), and these app suites: circle_centre, feature_pick, feature_pick_wire, mcp, mcp_setup, mcp_pick, mcp_live, one_wcs, setup_wcs, commands_undo, wcs_align, wcs_view_pose, face_origin, vertex_pick, pick.\n  - Not run: `cargo xtask gate quick` itself. Its dry run fell back to every crate, which is batch-sized.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Nobody has looked at the page in the real app (hand check below). No snapshot PNG changed. The release-lane `egui_shell_snapshot` was not run; the WCS page is not in that frame.\n- A circle on a rotated or aligned setup is covered by the view-pose transform, and the app test covers a translated part. No rotated-setup test was added.\n\n## Hand check\n\n1. Open the WCS node and check the three sections. Each field should sit on one row with its label. Narrow the properties pane: the turn buttons should stretch evenly, and the compass should stay centred with equal cells.\n2. Set *Anchor on: Circle centre*, then press *Pick a circular edge*. Hovering a hole rim or boss edge should highlight it. A click should move the WCS origin to the circle centre at the rim's height and show \"Circle Ø … , centre (…)\". Ctrl+Z should restore the previous origin.\n3. With the pick armed, click a straight edge: the status line and the page should say it is straight, and the origin should stay put.\n4. Switch back to Stock box: the compass and \"Pick markers in viewport\" should work as before.\n\nChangelog: WCS page: anchor the origin on the centre of a picked circular edge (hole rim or boss), undoable and with MCP tool `set_wcs_circle_centre`; page laid out in sections with one-row fields, even quarter-turn buttons and a 3x3 anchor compass\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #739\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
